From 207b0e4cc015271bd02a341feb73c49b05f0f2fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:46:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: RDNA4 kernels for the Flash-Next GSQ-RCO mixes (BF16
 hc, IQ2_S/IQ3_S/Q2_0)

ISTA-DASLab's Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GSQ-RCO quants keep the hyper-connection
weights in BF16 (the fused hc_mix path needs Q8_0, so they run as plain
BF16 mat-vecs: ~38 % of decode GPU time) and use IQ3_S / IQ2_S / IQ2_XXS /
Q2_0 experts. All changes are bit-exact.

- mul_mat_vec_f, HIP BF16: #pragma unroll 4 on the K loop (the F32 path
  already has it). Router 512x2560 14.8 -> 5.6 us, hc down 320x10240
  15.1 -> 11.8 us, inject 4x10240 6.4 -> 2.5 us.
- mul_mat_vec_f_vb (RDNA4): short rows (one K iteration per thread,
  K <= 512) and >= 3072 rows: one warp per row plays the original block's
  threads (same per-thread K order, same butterflies, same cross-warp sum),
  4 rows per block, at most 1792 warps (grid-size stall). Taken while
  (block_size/32) * ncols <= 36. hc up 10240x320: 23.6 -> 14.1 us (1 tok),
  36.7 -> 32.1 us (5 tok).
- IQ2_S / IQ3_S sign decode (mmvq vec dot and mmq tile loaders): the
  nibble-multiply apply_ksigns instead of __vcmpne4/__vsub4 (grid bytes are
  in [1, 127]). MoE mat-vec -10..-14 %, MoE mmq -6..-8 %.
- IQ3_S / IQ2_S join the RDNA4 one-token row loop (the faster dot product
  moved 6144..16384-row weights onto the stall sizes): dense -5..-42 %.
- IQ2_XXS / IQ2_S / Q2_0 experts take the RDNA4 routed-compact MoE mmq
  (as IQ2_XS / IQ3_XXS do): -11..-33 % at 64..2048 tokens.

GSQ IQ3_XXS (24 layers of experts on the CPU), GPU time vs r28 + the
dispatch-stall patch: decode -17.4 %, 5-token verify -10.7 %, prefill
-8.1 %. Greedy output identical (plain and MTP-drafted).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
